          %h2#Idea Idea
          .float_right_image{:style => "margin: -40px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/HardWallModelPredictions.jpg", :width => "440px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                From
                %a{:href => "#Erlich09"} Erlich 09, section 1.2
          %p
            What is called
            %em holographic QCD
            or
            %em AdS/QCD correspondence
            or similar (review includes
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Aharony02"} Aharony 02
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Erlich09"} Erlich 09
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#KimYi11"} Kim-Yi 11
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Erlich14"} Erlich 14
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Rebhan14"} Rebhan 14
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#RhoZahed16"} Rho-Zahed 16
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+theoretical+physics%29"} model
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+chromodynamics"} quantum chromodynamics
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"}> QCD
            ”, the
            = succeed "-sector" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+nuclear+force"} strong nuclear force
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT+correspondence"} AdS/CFT correspondence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary field theory
            of an (at least)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D5+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} 5-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bottom-up+model+building"} bottom-up
            holographic QCD”), specifically one
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+engineering"} geometrically engineered
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+model"} intersecting D-branes
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/top-down+model+building"} top-down
            holographic QCD”) and here specifically on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-D8+brane+intersections"} D4-D8 brane intersections
            (the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto+model"} Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto model
            due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Witten98"} Witten 98
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#KarchKatz02"} Karch-Katz 02
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#SakaiSugimoto04"} Sakai-Sugimoto 04
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#SakaiSugimoto05"} Sakai-Sugimoto 05
          %p#QCDNotManifestlyAnSCFT
            While
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            of the kind considered in the plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+correspondence"} AdS-CFT correspondence
            – since it is not a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+field+theory"} conformal field theory
            (but see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "confinement#KPV22"} KPV22
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetric
            (hence not an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SCFT"} SCFT
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron+supersymmetry"} hadron supersymmetry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} colors
            (but see
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#SmallNOpenProblem"} below
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT"} AdS-CFT
            may still usefully apply.
          %p
            Holographic QCD captures the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effect"} non-perturbative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confined
            regime of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass+gap+problem"} Mass Gap Millennium Problem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
            are all
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+state"} bound
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confined
            inside
            = succeed "-less" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} color
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadrons"} hadrons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meson"} meson
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
            instead being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
            of a
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+%28particle+physics%29"} flavour
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+perturbation+theory"} gauge theory
            (holographic dictionary, e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#KimYi11"} Kim-Yi 11 (3.1)
            = succeed "\u201D)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hidden+local+symmetry"} hidden local symmetry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
            being
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solitons"} solitons
            of this flavour/meson field, namely
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skyrmions"} skyrmions
          .float_right_image{:style => "margin: -40px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/IntersectingBranesSSWModel.jpg", :width => "600px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                From
                %a{:href => "#Rebhan14"} Rebhan 14
          %p
            This
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} dual
            description of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} color
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gluons"} gluons
            instead as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+%28particle+physics%29"} flavour
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mesons"} mesons
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+engineering+of+QFT"} geometrically brought out
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-D8+brane+intersections"} D4-D8 brane intersections
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto+model"} Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+model"} intersecting D-brane model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+strings"} open strings
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-branes"} D4
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+branes"} color branes
            give the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} color
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gluon"} gluon
            gauge field, while those on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D8-brane"} D8
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+branes"} flavor branes
            give the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+%28particle+physics%29"} flavour
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meson"} meson
            gauge field, those stretching between D4 and D8 give the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+strings"} closed strings
            give the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/glueballs"} glueballs
            %em
              %a{:href => "#WSSBraneConfiguration"} WSS brane configuration
            below.) This way
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} color
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+%28particle+physics%29"} flavor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+physics"} duality
            is mapped to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open%2Fclosed+string+duality"} open/closed string duality
            (as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D8-branes"} D8-branes
            are treated as probe branes).
          %p
            Notice that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+physics"} flavour sector
            is where most of the open problems regarding the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            are located (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+problem"}> flavour problem
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+anomalies"} flavour anomalies
          .float_right_image{:style => "margin: -40px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/SakaiSugimotoModel.jpg", :width => "570px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                From
                %a{:href => "#Erlich09"} Erlich 09, section 1.1
          %p
            Various fundamental characteristics of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            that remain mysterious in the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} colored
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quark"} quark
            model readily find a conceptual explanation in terms of this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+engineering+of+QFT"} geometric engineering
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+physics"} flavour physics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
            and of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+symmetry+breaking"} chiral symmetry breaking
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+meson+dominance"} vector meson dominance
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cheshire+cat+principle"} Cheshire cat principle
          .float_right_image{:style => "margin: -40px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/AdSCFTForQCD.jpg", :width => "600px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                From
                %a{:href => "#AHI12"} Aoki-Hashimoto-Iizuka 12
          %p
            Indeed, holographic QCD gives accurate quantitative predictions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confined
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron"} hadron
            spectra, hence of the physics of ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atomic+nuclei"} atomic nuclei
            (see comparison between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            and predictions of holographic QCD
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#BottomUpModels"} below
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbation theory
            and otherwise computable, at best, via the blind numerics of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+QCD"} lattice QCD
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Witten98"} Witten 98
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass+gap+problem"} mass gap problem
            (not yet a rigorous proof, but a proof strategy).
          %p
            Concretely, much of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phenomenology"} phenomenological
            success of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
            is (review in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#RhoZahed16"} Rho-Zahed 16, Chapter III
            %em ad hoc
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmion"} Skyrmion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+theoretical+physics%29"} model
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solitons"} solitons
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meson"} meson
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+%28particle+physics%29"} flavour
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
          %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/FirstEightSkyrmions.jpg", :width => "450px"}/
            %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
              From
              %a{:href => "Skyrmion#Manton11"} Manton 11
          %p
            Moreover, in holographic QCD this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmion"} Skyrmion
            model of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
            emerges in its modern improved form, where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pion"} pion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            is accompanied by the whole tower of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+mesons"} vector mesons
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rho+meson"} rho meson
            etc.): these
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meson"} meson
            species are holographically unified as the transversal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-mechanism"} KK-modes
            in the holographic theory. Already just adjoining the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rho+meson"} rho meson
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pion"} pion
            makes the resulting
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmions"} Skyrmions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nuclei"} nuclei
            all the way up to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/carbon"} carbon
            (
            %a{:href => "Skyrmion#NayaSutcliffe18a"}> Naya-Sutcliffe 18a
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "Skyrmion#NayaSutcliffe18b"} Naya-Sutcliffe 18b
          %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/SkyrmionsWithRho.jpg", :width => "540px"}/
            %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
              From
              %a{:href => "Skyrmion#NayaSutcliffe18"} Naya-Sutcliffe 18
          %p
            The mechanism behind this description of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nuclei"} nuclei
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
            is the theorem of
            %a{:href => "skyrmion#AtiyahManton89"} Atiyah-Manton 89
            (highlighted as such in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "skyrmion#Sutcliffe10"} Sutcliffe 10
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmions"} Skyrmions
            in 3+1-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+mechanism"} KK modes
            (transversal
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomies"} holonomies
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instantons"} instantons
            in 4+1-dimensional YM theory:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mtext baryons
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mover
                    %mo ↔
                    %mtext Skyrme
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                    %mrow
                      %mtext Skyrmions
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtext in
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi d
                        %mo =
                        %mn 3
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mover
                    %mo ↔
                    %mtext Atiyah-Manton
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                    %mrow
                      %mtext Instantons
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtext in
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi d
                        %mo =
                        %mn 4
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\text{baryons}
                  \\;\;
                  \\overset{\text{Skyrme}}{\leftrightarrow}
                  \\;\;
                  {
                  {\text{Skyrmions}}
                  \\atop
                  {\text{in}\; d=3+1}
                  }
                  \\;\;
                  \\overset{\text{Atiyah-Manton}}{\leftrightarrow}
                  \\;\;
                  {
                  {\text{Instantons}}
                  \\atop
                  {\text{in}\; d=4+1}
                  }
          %p
            This fact (of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phenomenology"} phenomenology
            on the left and of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            on the right) combined with the emergence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strings"} strings
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%27t+Hooft+limit"} 't Hooft limit
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            reveals a
            %em de facto
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT+correspondence"} holographic
            nature of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
            is to sort out the fine-print.
          %p#SmallNOpenProblem
            A key open problem here is that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT+correspondence"} AdS/CFT correspondence
            is currently well understood only in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+N+limit"} large N limit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_c
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} colors
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%27t+Hooft+coupling"} 't Hooft coupling
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            are both large. But for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            the number of colors is small,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi c
                    %mo =
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_c = 3
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+N+limit"} small N limit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+field+theory"} classical
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} super
            = succeed "-computations" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+N+limit"} small-N corrections
            (highlighted for holographic QCD e.g. in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Sugimoto16"} Sugimoto 16
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#StringAndMTheoryCorrection"} below
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theory"} perturbative string theory
            (for small
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%27t+Hooft+coupling"} 't Hooft coupling
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            (for small
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_c
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "M-theory#TheOpenProblem"} formulating M-theory remains an open problem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+N+limit"} small-N corrected
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass+gap+problem"} mass gap problem
            %a{:href => "confinement#OpenProblem"} confinement problem
            translates to the problem of formulating
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
          %center
            %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/Schreiber-MTheoryMathematics2020-v200126.pdf#page=8"}
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/ProblemQCDToProblemM230120.jpg", :width => "670"}/
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            From
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#Yi09"} Yi 09
          %blockquote
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              is a challenging theory. Its most interesting aspects, namely the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} color
              and the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+symmetry+breaking"} chiral symmetry breaking
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+gauge+theory"} lattice gauge theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              below the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scale"} scale
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
            %p
              it has been proposed early on that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
              are topological
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solitons"} solitons
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmions"} Skyrmions
              = succeed "but" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              the usual
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmion"} Skyrmion
              picture of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryon"} baryon
              has to be modified significantly in the context of full
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
            %p
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT"} holographic picture
              naturally brings a gauge principle in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk+spacetime"} bulk
              description of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+physics"} flavor
              dynamics in such a way that all spin one
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mesons"} mesons
              as well as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pions"} pions
              would enter the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmion"} skyrmionic
              = succeed "construction" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
              on the equal footing.
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
              is similar to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+perturbation+theory"} chiral perturbation theory
              in the sense that we deal with exclusively
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+invariance"} gauge-invariant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observables"} operators
              of the theory. The huge difference is, however, that this new approach tends to treat all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+invariance"} gauge-invariant
              objects together. Not only the light
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meson"} meson
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
              like
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pions"} pions
              but also heavy
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+mesons"} vector mesons
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
              appear together, at least in principle. In other words, a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
              deals with all
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} color
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+representation"} singlets
              simultaneously, giving us a lot more predictive power.
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
          %blockquote
            %p
              The expectation that there exists a more intelligent theory consisting only of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+invariance"} gauge-invariant
              objects in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+N+limit"} large Nc limit
              is thus realized via
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
              in a somewhat surprising manner that the master fields, those truly physical degrees of freedom, actually live not in four dimensional Minkowskian world but in five or higher dimensional curved geometry. This is not however completely unanticipated, and was heralded in the celebrated work by
              %a{:href => "#EguchiKawai82"} Eguchi and Kawai in early 1980’s
              which is all the more remarkable in retrospect.
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
            %p
              To compare against actual
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              = succeed "the" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%27t+Hooft+coupling"} 't Hooft coupling
              and the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+compactification"} KK
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scale"} scale
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              to fit both the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pion"} pion
              decay constant
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\pi
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
              of the first
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+meson"} vector meson
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/masses"} masses
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coupling+constants"} coupling constants
              are fixed. This version
              = succeed "the" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WSS+model"} WSS model
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
              is extremely predictive.
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              this
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              elevates the classic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skyrmion"} Skyrme picture
              based on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pions"} pions
              to a unified model involving all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+meson"} spin one mesons
              in addition to
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pions"} pions
            %p
              As we saw in this note, for low momentum processes, such as soft
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pion"} pion
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering+amplitude"} processes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rho+meson"} rho meson
              exchanges, and soft elastic scattering of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/photons"} photons
              = succeed "holographic" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WSS+model"} WSS
              = succeed "model\u2019s" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryon"} baryon
              sector works out almost as well as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meson"} meson
              sector
          %p
            %br/
          %p#FromSNM16
            From
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#SuganumaNakagawaMatsumoto16"} Suganuma-Nakagawa-Matsumoto 16, p. 1
          %blockquote
            %p
              Since 1973,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+chromodynamics"} quantum chromodynamics
              (QCD) has been established as the fundamental theory of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+nuclear+force"} strong interaction
            %p
              To analyze nonperturbative QCD, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+QCD"} lattice QCD
              Monte Carlo simulation has been also used as a first-principle calculation of the strong interaction. However, it has several weak points. For example, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+state"} state
              information (e.g. the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+function"} wave function
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+QCD"} lattice QCD
              is based on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path-integral"} path-integral
              formalism. Also, it is difficult to take the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+fermion"} chiral
              limit, because zero-mass
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pions"} pions
              require
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+volume+limit"} infinite volume lattices
              = succeed "\u201D" do
                %a{:href => "lattice+gauge+theory#SignProblem"} sign problem
            %p
              On the other hand,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
              has a direct connection to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
              is equivalent to infrared QCD in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+N+limit"} large Nc
              and strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%27t+Hooft+coupling"} 't Hooft coupling
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge%2Fgravity+correspondence"} gauge/gravity correspondence
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
              is successful to reproduce many
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron"} hadron
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phenomenology"} phenomenology
              such as
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+meson+dominance"} vector meson dominance
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skyrmion"} Skyrme soliton picture
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+QCD"} lattice QCD
              simulations, holographic QCD is usually formulated in the chiral limit, and does not have the
              %a{:href => "lattice+gauge+theory#SignProblem"} sign problem
              at finite density.
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            From
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#RhoEtAl16"} Rho et a. 16
          %blockquote
            %p
              One can make
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+perturbation+theory"} chiral perturbation theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              consistent with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              by suitably matching the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correlators"} correlators
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective theory
              to those of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              at a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scale"} scale
              near
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+mesons"} vector mesons
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fields"} gauge fields
              in an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang–Mills
              type form. We will see in Part III that such a structure arises,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/top-down+model+building"} top-down
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              model comes out to describe — unexpectedly well — low-energy properties of both
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mesons"} mesons
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+QCD"} lattice QCD
              simulations.
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
            %p
              One of the most noticeable results of this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FQCD"} holographic model
              is the first derivation of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+meson+dominance"} vector dominance
              (VD) that holds both for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mesons"} mesons
              and for
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jun+John+Sakurai"} Sakurai's
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+meson+dominance"} vector dominance
              — with the lowest
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+mesons"} vector mesons
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rho+meson"} ρ
              and ω — which held very well for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pion"} pionic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/form+factors"} form factors
              at low momentum transfers famously failed for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nucleon"} nucleon
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/form+factors"} form factors
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FQCD"} holographic model
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+meson+dominance"} VD
              comes out automatically for both the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pion"} pion
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nucleon"} nucleon
              provided that the infinite
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+mechanism"} KK-
              = succeed "tower" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+meson+dominance"} VD
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pion"} pion
              with the infinite tower is not surprising given the successful Sakurai VD, that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+meson+dominance"} VD
              holds also for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nucleons"} nucleons
              is highly nontrivial.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
              It turns out to be a consequence of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FQCD"} holographic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cheshire+cat+principle"} Cheshire Cat phenomenon
          %p
            %br/
          %div
            %h2#PolyakovGaugeStringDualitySection Polyakov gauge/string duality
            %p
              Key ideas underlying what is now known as
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+correspondence"} holographic
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} duality in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
              and specifically as
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-QCD+correspondence"} holographic QCD
              (see also at
              = succeed ")" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+light+front+QCD"} holographic light front QCD
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"} Alexander Polyakov
              (cf. historical reminiscences in
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#Polyakov08"} Polyakov (2008)
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge%2Fstring+duality"} gauge/string duality
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confined
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              (the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass+gap+problem"} mass gap problem
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} color
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+tubes"} flux tubes
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+lines"}> Wilson lines
              ) between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
              as dynamical
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strings"} strings
            %p
              The logic here proceeds in the following steps (cf.
              %a{:href => "#Polyakov07"} Polyakov (2007), §1
              and see the commentary
              = succeed "):" do
                %a{:href => "#NoticeTheDecisiveInsight"} below
            .float_right_image{:style => "margin: 0px 0px 10px 15px"}
              %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
                %img{:src => "/nlab/files/HadronicStringInPionScattering.jpg", :width => "400px"}/
                %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                  From
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "string+theory#Veneziano12"} Veneziano 2012
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %strong flux tubes confine as dynamical strings
                %p
                  The starting point is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypothesis"} hypothesis
                  that the strong coupling of particles (such as
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
                  (such as the
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+nuclear+force"} strong nuclear force
                  = succeed "\u201D" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+tubes"} flux tubes
                  = succeed "\u201D)" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+lines"} Wilson lines
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strings"} strings
                  with a given
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tension"} tension
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "#KogutSusskind74"} Kogut &amp; Susskind (1974)
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a{:href => "#KogutSusskind75"} (1975)
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a{:href => "#Wilson74"} Wilson (1974)
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "#Polyakov79"} Polyakov (1979)
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "#Polyakov80"} (1980)
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a{:href => "#Polyakov80"} (1987)
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "#MakeenkoMigdal81"} Makeenko &amp; Migdal (1981)
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "Nambu-Goto+action#Nambu70"} Nambu (1970)
                  %a{:href => "Nambu-Goto+action#Gotō71"} Gotō (1971)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
                %p Under this assumption it would be:
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      the
                      = succeed "/" do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+tube"} flux tube
                      = succeed "\u2018s" do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string"} string
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tension"} tension
                      which keeps the particles at theirs endpoints
                      = succeed "," do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confined
                  %li
                    %p
                      the excitation of these
                      = succeed "/" do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+tubes"} flux tubes
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strings"} strings
                      which follow
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Regge+trajectories"} Regge trajectories
                      (such as of
                      = succeed ");" do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadrons"} hadrons
                  %li
                    %p
                      the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering"} scattering
                      of these
                      = succeed "/" do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+tubes"} flux tubes
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strings"} strings
                      which explains the observed
                      = succeed "," do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Veneziano+amplitudes"} Veneziano amplitudes
                %p which are the main qualitative features to be explained.
              %li#QuantumFluxTubesProbeHigherDim
                %p
                  %strong quantum flux tubes probe effective higher dimensions
                %p
                  But if so, famous quantum effects make such
                  = succeed "/" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+tubes"} flux tubes
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strings"} strings
                  behave like propagating in an effective/emergent higher-dimensional spacetime:
                %ul
                  %li
                    either because one regards the string as
                    %em a priori
                    propagating in non-critical
                    = succeed "-" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mn 4
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4
                    = succeed "/" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dilaton+field"} dilaton field
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Liouville+field"} Liouville field
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ϕ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                    appears to cancel the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+anomaly"} quantum anomaly
                    and acts like a warped 5th dimension:
                %p
                  this was the point of view published in
                  %a{:href => "#Polyakov81"} Polyakov (1981)
                  but later claimed, in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "#Polyakov08"} Polyakov (2008)
                %ul
                  %li
                    or because one regards the string as propagating in critical dimension (10 for the
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
                %p
                  which is the point of view adopted later in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+duality"} AdS-CFT duality
                  %a{:href => "AdS-CFT+correspondence#Maldacena97a"} Maldacena (1997)
                %p
                  with only the endpoints of the
                  = succeed "/" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+tube"} flux tube
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string"} string
                  constrained to lie in the original lower dimensional spacetime
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "#Polyakov98"} Polyakov (1998)
                  %a{:href => "#Polyakov99"} (1999)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
                %p
                  which now appears (in modern language that Polyakov did not originally use) as a “
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"}> brane
                  ” inside a higher dimensional
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
                  spacetime.
                %blockquote
                  %p
                    Notice that in this picture the observable physics that we set out to describe takes place
                    %em on the brane
                    (
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
                    which is typically flat
                    = succeed "!)" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+boundary"} asymptotic
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
                    of a higher-dimensional
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
                    spacetime, while the (potentially large) extra dimensions of a possibly
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∼
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim
                    = succeed "-bulk" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS"} AdS
                    %em thickness
                    of the
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+tube"} flux tube
                    = succeed "cf." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                    %a{:href => "#Polyakov08"} Polyakov (2008), p. 3
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %li
                %p
                  %strong
                    large/small
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi N
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
                    confined gauge theory is holographic string theory/M-theory
                %p
                  Thus the description of strongly coupled matter via
                  = succeed "/" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+tubes"} flux tubes
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strings"} strings
                  now reveals a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holography"} holographic
                  situation where strongly-coupled quantum fields on
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+brane+models"} intersecting branes
                  are equivalently described by a theory of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"} quantum gravity
                  mediated by
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strings"} strings
                  propagating in a higher dimensional
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
                %p
                  In relation to gauge string duality this is due to
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "#GubserKlebanovPolyakov98"} Gubser, Klebanov &amp; Polyakov (1998)
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT+duality"} AdS/CFT duality
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "#PolyakovRychkov00"} Polyakov &amp; Rychkov (2000)
            %blockquote
              %p
                While this dual bulk string theory is itself strongly-coupled unless the “number of coincident branes” is humongous (the “
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large-N+limit"}> large-N limit
                ”) and thus unrealistic after all, the difference is that recognizing the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
                as physical objects reveals a web of concrete hints as to the string’s strongly-coupled (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+quantum+field+theory"}> non-perturbative
                ) completion, going under the working title
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "AdS-CFT+correspondence#SmallNCorrections"}
                      AdS-CFT – Small
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi N
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
                      corrections
              %p
                In summary, the plausible approach of understanding strongly-coupled quantum gauge theories by regarding their
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+tubes"} flux tubes
                as dynamical
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strings"} strings
                seems to recast the
                %a{:href => "mass+gap#ReferencesMassGapProblem"} Millennium Problem
                of understanding strongly-coupled matter into the problem of formulating
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+brane+models"} intersecting brane models
                of single (or a small number of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coincident+branes"} coincident
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-branes"} M-branes
                (such as the
                %em
                  %a{:href => "AdS-QCD+correspondence#WittenSakaiSugimotoModel"} Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto model
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
                system) on whose
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
                the desired strongly-coupled field theory is realized (such as
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            %p#NoticeTheDecisiveInsight
              Notice the decisive early insight of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"} Alexander Polyakov
              here: While the idea that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strings"} strings
              somehow describe
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron"} hadronic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+states"} bound states
              was the very origin of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
              in the early 1970s (“dual resonance models”), the mainstream
              %em abandoned
              this perspective in the later 1970s when the critical dimension and the full spectrum of the string became fully understood (cf.
              = succeed ")" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goddard-Thorn+no-ghost+theorem"} Goddard-Thorn no-ghost theorem
              %em instead
              string should be understood as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GUT"} grand unified
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+of+everything"} theory of everything
              including
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"} quantum gravity
              (see e.g. the historical review of
              %a{:href => "string+theory#Veneziano12"} Veneziano (2012), esp. pp. 30-31
              which still clings to this perspective). From here it was only through the long detour of first discovering, inside this grander theory:
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
              (and
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/near-horizon+geometry"} near-horizon
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+duality"} AdS-CFT duality
              just before the 2000s and then another decade of exploring
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+models"} intersecting D-brane models
              that the community in the 2010s came back full circle to Polyakov’s holographic perspective on
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strings"} strings
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+tubes"} flux tubes
              that propagate not (alone) in the observable 4 spacetime dimensions but in a primarily unobservable (meanwhile known as
              = succeed "-like)" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Randall-Sundrum+model"} Randall-Sundrum
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
              spacetime – a holographic description of reality that
              %a{:href => "#Polyakov99"} Polyakov (1999)
              referred to as the
              = succeed "," do
                %em wall of the cave
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Plato"} Plato
              (cf. also
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Polyakov08"} Polyakov (2008), p. 6
            %p
              Our whereabouts in this remarkable picture are still often misunderstood today: If string theory is a theory of nature, then, it seems, we see the wall but not the cave: we live on a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowskian
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+model"} brane intersection
              at the (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+boundary"}> asympotic
              )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
              of a primarily unobserved
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetime"} anti de Sitter
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
              – which may better be thought of not as physical space but as a configuration space of quantum flux.
          %p
            %br/
          %h2#Models Models
          %p
            In approaches to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi AdS
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi QCD
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS/QCD
            one distinguishes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/top-down+model+building"} top-down model building
            – where the ambition is to first set up a globally consistent ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+model"} intersecting D-brane model
            where a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            at least similar to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            arises on suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+engineering+of+gauge+theories"}> geometric engineering of gauge theories
            ) – from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bottom-up+model+building"} bottom-up model building
            approaches which are more cavalier about global consistency and first focus on accurately fitting the intended
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phenomenology"} phenomenology
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+boundary"} asymptotic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary field theory
            of
            = succeed "+" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
            on some
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetime"} anti de Sitter spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+theoretical+physics%29"} model
            which is both
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} realistic
            as well as globally consistent as a
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+vacuum"} string vacuum
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} string phenomenology
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/BottomUpAndTopDownIntersDBraneModelBuilding.png", :width => "700"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics from
              %a{:href => "bottom-up+and+top-down+model+building#AldazabalIbanezQuevedoUranga00"} Aldazabal-Ibáñez-Quevedo-Uranga 00
          %h3#TopDownModels Top-down models
          %h4#WittenSakaiSugimotoModel Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto model
          %p
            A good
            = succeed "-approach" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/top-down+model+building"} top-down model building
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#SakaiSugimoto04"} Sakai-Sugimoto 04
            %a{:href => "#SakaiSugimoto05"} Sakai-Sugimoto 05
            based on
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Witten98"} Witten 98
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Rebhan14"} Rebhan 14
            %a{:href => "#Sugimoto16"} Sugimoto 16
            for review.
          %h5#WSSBraneConfiguration Brane configuration
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto+model"} Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+engineering+of+QFT"} geometrically engineers
            something at least close to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+models"} coincident
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/near+horizon+geometry"} near horizon geometry
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi AdS
                    %mn 7
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_7 \times S^4
            in the decoupling limit where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            theory becomes the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+%282%2C0%29-superconformal+SCFT"} 6d (2,0)-superconformal SCFT
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            is on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"} torus
            with anti-periodic boundary conditions for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermions"} fermions
            in one direction, thus
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spontaneous+symmetry+breaking"} breaking
            all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Scherk-Schwarz+mechanism"}> Scherk-Schwarz mechanism
            ), where the first circle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} reduction
            realizes, under
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+M-theory+and+type+IIA+string+theory"} duality between M-theory and type IIA string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
            as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-branes"} D4-branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            further
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} compactified
            on a circle. (
            %a{:href => "#Witten98"}> Witten 98, section 4
            ).
          %p
            The further introduction of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+model"} intersecting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D8-branes"} D8-branes
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+D-brane"} anti
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D8-branes"} D8-branes
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-D8+brane+bound+states"} D4-D8 brane bound states
            makes a sensible sector of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+fermions"} chiral fermions
            appear in this model (
            %a{:href => "#SakaiSugimoto04"}> Sakai-Sugimoto 04
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#SakaiSugimoto05"} Sakai-Sugimoto 05
          %p#BraneConfigurationDiagram
            The following diagram indicates the Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+model"} intersecting D-brane model
            that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+engineering+of+QFT"} geometrically engineers
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/WSSBraneConfigurationEngineeringQCDII.jpg", :width => "740"}/
          %div{:style => "float:right;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/D8D6NS5.jpg", :width => "380"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Differential+Cohomotopy+implies+intersecting+brane+observables"} Sati-Schreiber 19c
          %p Here we are showing:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+brane"} color
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-branes"} D4-branes
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+brane"} flavor
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D8-branes"} D8-branes
              %p with
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/5d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 5d Chern-Simons theory
                    on their
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
                %li
                  %p
                    the corresponding
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4d+WZW+model"} 4d WZW model
                    on the boundary
              %p
                exhibiting the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+meson+fields"} vector meson fields
                in the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmion+model"} Skyrmion model
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryon"} baryon
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-branes"} D4-branes
              %p
                (see below at
                = succeed ");" do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "#Baryons"} Baryons
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+monopole"} Yang-Mills monopole
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
              %p
                (see at
                = succeed ");" do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-D8-brane+bound+state"} D6-D8-brane bound state
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-branes"} NS5-branes
                (often not considered here).
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Differential+Cohomotopy+implies+intersecting+brane+observables"} Sati-Schreiber 19c
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            %br/
          %h5#WSSModelGlueballs Glueballs
          %p
            Already before adding the D8-branes (hence already in the pure Witten model) this produces a pure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            whose
            = succeed "-spectra" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/glueball"} glueball
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/GlueballSpectrumSSWModel.jpg", :width => "700"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics from
              %a{:href => "#Rebhan14"} Rebhan 14
          %h5#Hadrons Hadrons
          %p
            In this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto+model"} Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto model
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effect"} strongly coupled
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadrons"} hadrons
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            correspond to
            = succeed "-phenomena" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string-theoretic
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk+field+theory"} bulk field theory
          %h6#mesons Mesons
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mesons"} mesons
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+states"} bound states
            of 2
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+strings"} open strings
            in the bulk, whose two endpoints on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+boundary"} asymptotic boundary
            correspond to the two quarks
          %h6#Baryons Baryons
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+states"} bound states
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_c
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Sugimoto16"} Sugimoto 16, 15.4.1
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                as
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wrapped+brane"} wrapped
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-branes"} D4-branes
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_c
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+strings"} open strings
                connecting them to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D8-brane"} D8-brane
              %p
                (
                %a{:href => "#Witten98b"}> Witten 98b
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#GrossOoguri98"} Gross-Ooguri 98, Sec. 5
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#BISY98"} BISY 98
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "#CGS98"} CGS98
            %li
              %p
                as
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skyrmions"} skyrmions
              %p
                (
                %a{:href => "#SakaiSugimoto04"}> Sakai-Sugimoto 04, section 5.2
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#SakaiSugimoto05"} Sakai-Sugimoto 05, section 3.3
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#Bartolini17"} Bartolini 17
          %p
            For review see
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Sugimoto16"} Sugimoto 16
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Yi09"} Yi 09
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Yi11"} Yi 11
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Yi13"} Yi 13
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Rebhan14"} Rebhan 14, around (18)
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/BaryonsAsD4Branes.jpg", :width => "700"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics from
              %a{:href => "#Sugimoto16"} Sugimoto 16
          %p
            Equivalently, these baryon states are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+instantons"} Yang-Mills instantons
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D8-brane"} D8-brane
            giving the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-D8+brane+bound+state"} D4-D8 brane bound state
            (
            %a{:href => "#SakaiSugimoto04"}> Sakai-Sugimoto 04, 5.7
            ) as a special case of the general situation for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dp-D%28p%2B4%29-brane+bound+states"} Dp-D(p+4)-brane bound states
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "Dp-D%28p%2B4%29-brane+bound+state#Tong05"} Tong 05, 1.4
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/BaryonVertexDefectInAdSQCD.jpg", :width => "490"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics from
              %a{:href => "#CaiLi17"} Cai-Li 17
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/D6InD8InAdSQCD.jpg", :width => "700"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics from
              %a{:href => "#ABBCN18"} ABBCN 18
          %p
            This already produces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryon"} baryon
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            spectra with moderate quantitative agreement with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            (
            %a{:href => "#HSSY07"}> HSSY 07
            ):
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/BaryonSpectrumInSakaiSugimoto.jpg", :width => "700"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics from
              %a{:href => "#Sugimoto16"} Sugimoto 16
          %p
            Moreover, the above 4-brane model for baryons is claimed to be equivalent to the old
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmion"} Skyrmion
              model
            (see
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#SakaiSugimoto04"} Sakai-Sugimoto 04, section 5.2
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#SakaiSugimoto05"} Sakai-Sugimoto 05, section 3.3
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Sugimoto16"} Sugimoto 16, 15.4.1
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Bartolini17"} Bartolini 17
          %p
            But the Skyrmion model of baryons has been shown to apply also to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+states"} bound states
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atomic+nuclei"} atomic nuclei
            (
            %a{:href => "Skyrmion#Riska93"}> Riska 93
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "Skyrmion#BattyeMantonSutcliffe10"} Battye-Manton-Sutcliffe 10
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "Skyrmion#Manton16"} Manton 16
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "Skyrmion#NayaSutcliffe18"} Naya-Sutcliffe 18
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atomic+number"} atomic number
          %p
            For instance, various
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experimentally
            observed resonances of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/carbon"} carbon
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nucleus"} nucleus
            are modeled well by a Skyrmion with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atomic+number"} atomic number
            6 and hence baryon number 12 (
            %a{:href => "Skyrmion#LauMaonton14"}> Lau-Manton 14
            ):
          %div{:style => "text-align: center"}
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/SkyrmionB12.jpg", :width => "200"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics form
              %a{:href => "Skyrmion#LauMaonton14"} Lau-Manton 14
          %p
            More generally, the
            = succeed "-model" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmion"} Skyrmion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atomic+nuclei"} atomic nuclei
            gives good matches with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            if not just the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pi+meson"} pi meson
            but also the
            = succeed "-background" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rho+meson"} rho meson
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "Skyrmion#NayaSutcliffe18"} Naya-Sutcliffe 18
          %div{:style => "text-align: center"}
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/SkyrmionsWithRho.jpg", :width => "800"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics form
              %a{:href => "Skyrmion#NayaSutcliffe18"} Naya-Sutcliffe 18
          %p
            %br/
          %h4#WSSTypeModelFor2dQCD WSS-type model for 2d QCD
          %p
            There is a direct analogue for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+QCD"} 2d QCD
            of the
            %a{:href => "#WittenSakaiSugimotoModel"} above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WSS+model"} WSS model
            for 4d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            (
            %a{:href => "#GaoXuZeng06"}> Gao-Xu-Zeng 06
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#YeeZahed11"} Yee-Zahed 11
          %p
            The corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+model"} intersecting D-brane model
            is much as that for 4d QCD
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#WSSBraneConfiguration"} above
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colour+charge"} color
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D2-branes"} D2-branes
                instead of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-branes"} D4-branes
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryon"} baryon
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
                instead of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-branes"} D4-branes
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meson"} meson
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
                given by 3d
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
                instead of
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/5d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 5d Chern-Simons theory
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/WSSBraneConfigurationEngineering2dQCD.jpg", :width => "740"}/
          %h4#Type0StringCorrespondence
            Type0B/
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi YM
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} YM_4
            \-correspondence
          %p
            Instead of starting with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} locally supersymmetric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            and then
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spontaneously+broken+symmetry"} spontaneously breaking
            all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            by suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            as in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#WittenSakaiSugimotoModel"} Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk+field+theory"} bulk
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            in the first place.
          %p
            In this vein, it has been argued in
            %a{:href => "#GLMR00"} GLMR 00
            that there is holographic duality between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+0+string+theory"} type 0 string theory
            and non-supersymmetric 4d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            (hence potentially something close to
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AAS19"} AAS 19
          %h3#BottomUpModels Bottom-up models
          %p
            A popular
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bottom-up+model+building"} bottom-up approach
            of AdS/QCD is known as the
            %em hard-wall model
            (
            %a{:href => "#ErlichKatzSonStephanov05"}> Erlich-Katz-Son-Stephanov 05
            ).
          %p
            Further refinement to the “soft-wall model” is due to
            %a{:href => "#KKSS06"} KKSS 06
            and further to “improved holographic QCD” is due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GursoyKiritsisNitti07"} Gursoy-Kiritsis-Nitti 07
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GursoyKiritsis08"} Gursoy-Kiritsis 08
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#GKMMN10"} GKMMN 10
          %h2#ComparisonWithExperiment Comparison with experiment
          %p
            Comparison of holographic QCD models with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            (mostly using bottom-up models).
          %p
            Computations due to
            %a{:href => "#KatzLewandowskiSchwartz05"} Katz-Lewandowski-Schwartz 05
            using the hard-wall model (
            %a{:href => "#ErlichKatzSonStephanov05"}> Erlich-Katz-Son-Stephanov 05
            ) find the following comparison of AdS/QCD predictions to
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/HardWallModelPredictions.jpg", :width => "400"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics from
              %a{:href => "#Erlich09"} Erlich 09, section 1.2
          %p
            Computations due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#KKSS06"} KKSS 06
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GursoyKiritsisNitti07"} Gursoy-Kiritsis-Nitti 07
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GursoyKiritsis08"} Gursoy-Kiritsis 08
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#GKMMN10"} GKMMN 10
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/GlueballMasses.jpg", :width => "660"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics from
              %a{:href => "#GKMMN10"} GKMMN 10
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/ImprovedAdSQCD.jpg", :width => "680"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics from
              %a{:href => "#GKMMN10"} GKMMN 10
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            From
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#PomarolWulzer09"} Pomarol-Wulzer 09
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/PomarolHolographicBaryonMasses.jpg", :width => "500"}/
          %p
            %br/
          %p#TablesdRocha21
            From
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#daRocha21"} da Rocha 21
            = succeed ":" do
